---
import ThreeFiguresPanel from "./why-we-exist/ThreeFiguresPanel.astro";

/*
 * Section 2 — why ArkSystems exists. Copy verbatim from docs/about-page.md.
 *
 * "THE TOOLS AREN'T THE CONSTRAINT" AND THE CLOSING LINE ARE POSITIONS, NOT CLAIMS, and
 * the copy file's claims section says so. Neither carries a figure or an attribution,
 * which is what keeps them inside the claims rules and what gives the page a point of
 * view at all. Do not add a statistic to either.
 *
 * "A GUESS WITH AN INVOICE ATTACHED" WAS CUT FROM THE HOMEPAGE AND IS DELIBERATE HERE.
 * On Aug 25 2026 the homepage's section 2 lede closed on that phrase and Fredrick
 * replaced it: on that page it landed as a diagnosis of the reader's own spending, in
 * the second section, before they had agreed to anything — which put them on the
 * defensive exactly where the page needed agreement. Here it does a different job. The
 * section is titled "why ArkSystems exists", the subject is AI investment in general
 * rather than this reader's, and nobody is being told their spending failed. It was
 * flagged to Fredrick before this page was built and kept on his approval. If it ever
 * reads as an accusation again, it goes — but do not delete it as a duplicate of the
 * homepage fix, because it is not one.
 *
 * IT NOW CARRIES A PANEL, and the reason is worth recording. Built first as a heading
 * and two paragraphs across a two-column head, it was the weakest band on the page —
 * Fredrick read it and said it looked like something that could be removed. He was right
 * about the symptom: this section makes the page's only abstract claim, that three
 * figures are missing, and abstract claims in prose are the easiest thing on a page to
 * skip. The panel is those three figures with nothing in them, which is the argument made
 * visible rather than asserted.
 *
 * THE LAYOUT IS SPLIT BY CONTENT TYPE — all the prose in column one, the panel in column
 * two — which is the site's standing rule for a two-column section. The heading moved
 * into the prose column with the paragraphs; it is no longer a two-column head.
 *
 * See why-we-exist/ThreeFiguresPanel.astro for why the panel must stay empty, and why it
 * is not the process diagram the copy file forbids.
 */
---

<section class="section section--cream why" id="why-we-exist">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="why__grid">
      <div class="why__copy">
        <h2 class="section__title why__title">The tools aren&rsquo;t the constraint.</h2>

        <div class="why__body">
        <p class="why__para">
          AI capability is now available to any business that wants it, at a price that no
          longer decides anything. The constraint is that most businesses can&rsquo;t
          identify where AI produces a return in their own operation, what that return is
          worth, or what capturing it would cost. Without those three figures, an AI
          investment is a guess with an invoice attached.
        </p>

        <p class="why__para why__para--second">
          ArkSystems exists to establish those three figures and to build what follows
          from them. The order is deliberate: assessment first, business case second,
          build only if the case holds.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="why__panel">
        <ThreeFiguresPanel />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .why__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(0, 0.95fr);
    column-gap: 64px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .why__title {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .why__para {
    font-size: var(--ark-body-lg);
    line-height: var(--ark-lh-body);
    color: var(--ark-body-ink);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .why__para--second {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .why__body {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  /* The heading centres on phone and in portrait, matching every other heading on the
   * site. It used to get this free from `.section__head` in base.css; that wrapper is
   * gone, so it is set here. */
  @media (max-width: 900px), (orientation: portrait) {
    .why__title {
      text-align: center;
      margin-inline: auto;
      max-width: 20ch;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    /* One column, in DOM order: the argument, then the picture of it. */
    .why__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .why__panel {
      margin-top: 30px;
    }

    .why__body {
      margin-top: 18px;
    }

    /* The block centres under the centred heading; the text inside stays left. Centred
     * prose is harder to read, which matters more than usual on a page written for
     * readers whose first language may not be English.
     *
     * This was a real bug once: while the heading and paragraphs shared a `.section__head`
     * wrapper, base.css centred everything in it and un-centred exactly one class,
     * `.section__lede`. These paragraphs are not that class, so they inherited the
     * centring and shipped centred. The wrapper is gone now, but the rule stays explicit —
     * any section putting body copy under a class other than `.section__lede` has to set
     * this for itself. */
    .why__para {
      text-align: left;
      margin-inline: auto;
      font-size: 1.0625rem;
      max-width: 44ch;
    }

    .why__para--second {
      margin-top: 14px;
    }
  }
</style>
